                <pb facs="0848" n="772" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg772"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5431/263a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-20T20:00:00-05:00">November 20, 1935—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>77. No word has been received regarding requirements set forth in the
                    Department’s 66, October 23, 2 p.m. We are wondering why, since enough time has
                    elapsed for the Swiss to have studied our proposed concessions and requests.</p>
                <p>Suggest that you endeavor to ascertain from Stucki causes for delay.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
